{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
  "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Beth S. Brinkmann",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The ruling of the Illinois Appellate Court in this case radically expanded the Court's operational-function tax. The State tax at issue violates the principles of constitutional limitations on state taxing authority for at least two reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You are saying to me, Ms. Brinkmann -- we talk about an asset, an investment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument next in Case 06-1413, MeadWestvaco v. The Illinois Department of Revenue. Ms. Brinkmann."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Don't we start -- I don't\nmean to cut off your argument, but don't we start with\nthe assumption that this is not a unitary business?\nWasn't that the finding of the trial court which was not\ndisturbed on appeal?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I don't like to intrude on\nthe white light, but if I could just ask one question.\nIf the unitary-tax argument has been\npreserved and is met and if there's a finding that they\nare unitary, does Illinois have the right to tax\nthe sale, or to -- to a portion of it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask this question just -- it shows my ignorance, but if the unitary-business approach to taxation was not applied in this case, how did you compute the amount of the tax?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Barov",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BAROV: Right. You use a different formula. You use a two-factor formula, but it was just related to Mead's sales, not to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, that's why it's even more dramatic to me that you didn't raise the argument based on the Lexis connection to Illinois."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Was there any sort of stipulation between the parties to say what each, what Lexis/Nexis was doing in Illinois, what Mead was doing in Illinois?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Barov",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BAROV: There was, there was a long stipulation, yes, Your Honor, and plus there was exhibits attached to the stipulation, which are reflected in our briefs, that discuss in detail what Mead and Lexis were both doing, at least their relationship to each other."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: If Illinois -- if Ohio is, in fact, taxing the whole gain at its full rate on the theory that this entire income should be allocated to Ohio, then you do have an element of double taxation, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Barov",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I think the Mobil Oil case should have disposed of that, that contention, because this Court rejected a similar argument that the mere possibility of taxation by a domiciliary State foreclosed taxation by a State where the business was present."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You're taxing Mead, not Nexis/Lexis?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Brinkmann",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BRINKMANN: There are facts, Your Honor, but the Illinois law is very clear; it's rule 341(h)(7) and (i) which applies to applee. If you don't raise a point in the appellate court, it is waived. That's an independent and adequate State ground. And it's a very breathtaking argument, as Justice Scalia pointed out, that also wasn't brought forth in the brief in opposition. Thank you, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "7a06624cf9c524c78a424c4bdc2f948806413eae4416d361f51e00b3b88aa698",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7a06624cf9c5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Initially, it's about the context in which -- what I regard as an important fact -- was raised, whether it was raised in the context of an argument on unitary business or whether or not they went too far, but the stubborn fact is still there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1413",
      "confidence": 0.0,
